Guy Weekly says NVIDIA used supercomputing 2026 to tee up Rubin HPC for scientists, engineers

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:37.840
and analysts working large data sets, and the current Rubin tops out at 28,672 CUDA cores.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.560
NVIDIA is calling the new part a balanced design, with NV-Link 7 keeping the 3.6 terabytes

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.880
per second of per GPU bandwidth already shipping on NV-Link 6.

