00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:10.004
The Trump administration moved to restrict foreign countries from giving Chinese companies

00:01:10.004 --> 00:01:16.244
remote access to advanced AI chips and servers, Bloomberg reports, amid scrutiny of export

00:01:16.244 --> 00:01:19.424
controls after an alleged NVIDIA espionage scandal.

00:01:19.924 --> 00:01:24.884
An interim Commerce Department rule says several Southeast Asian nations, along with

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:30.144
Brazil, will need a U.S. government license to buy advanced AI chips from NVIDIA and other

00:01:30.144 --> 00:01:31.304
American manufacturers.

00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:36.037
NVIDIA's own board answered the control problem with a standing committee.

00:01:36.637 --> 00:01:40.997
The National Security and Export Control Oversight Committee will watch national security

00:01:40.997 --> 00:01:47.217
policy, export control compliance, and global trade risk, chaired by director Suzanne Nora

00:01:47.217 --> 00:01:53.237
Johnson, with Steven C. Neal and John O. DeBerry beside her. It meets at least quarterly, with

00:01:53.237 --> 00:01:58.057
management and an executive session, and it will keep independent outside experts in law,

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:03.397
national security, and trade compliance. The national security team and the global trade

00:02:03.397 --> 00:02:08.317
compliance team report to that committee, and to interim chief executive Collette Cress on

00:02:08.317 --> 00:02:13.517
day-to-day work. Chairman Harvey Jones said NVIDIA has a responsibility to help safeguard

00:02:13.517 --> 00:02:19.137
national security while innovation continues. The financial time says the step comes as Washington

00:02:19.137 --> 00:02:24.997
criticizes NVIDIA's ambition to grow revenue in China. After the U.S. moved to cut off China's

00:02:24.997 --> 00:02:31.665
access to the company's most powerful AI chips. Apple is close to a long DRAM contract that breaks

00:02:31.665 --> 00:02:37.965
